  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607196200: Typed PostgreSQL SQLSTATE metadata

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

`pg_query_state` metadata is seven bytes: result kind, ReadyForQuery state, and
the exact five-byte SQLSTATE from ErrorResponse field `C`. Error results
without exactly one bounded five-byte SQLSTATE fail closed. Successful results
write five zero bytes. The component still returns the bounded validated raw
response so applications may inspect additional fields without expanding the
trusted linker ABI.

The fixed-size independent-memory copy-out is seven bytes and remains checked
against consumer capacity. Released PostgreSQL qualification intentionally
causes division-by-zero and requires SQLSTATE `22012` together with state
sequence `T`, `E`, `I`.

This supersedes ADR-2607196100's two-byte metadata decision. Typed localized
message/detail/hint extraction remains outside the control-flow contract;
prepared statements, cancellation, pooling and production matrices remain
open.")))
